# Phenotype-org standard consumer justfile (v2 / 2026-06-14)
#
# Source: https://github.com/KooshaPari/phenotype-tooling/blob/main/templates/justfile
#
# This is a thin shell that re-exports the shared `phenotype.just` library.
# The 17 recipes that consumers used to copy-paste
# (default, build, test, lint, fmt, audit, unused, typecheck, outdated, update,
#  coverage, sbom, license, version, ci, docs, dev, clean, info, doctor,
#  benchmark, fuzz, release-dryrun) are now defined once in
# `phenotype.just` and parameterized over the build system.
#
# Stack-specific recipes (e.g. `register-startmenu` for Electrobun desktop
# apps, `migrate` for Django, `db-reset` for Rails) stay in THIS file.
# Add new stack-specific recipes here; do not modify `phenotype.just` from
# a consumer repo.
#
# Changes from v1 (2026-06-11):
#   * imports the v2 shared library which adds outdated/update/coverage/sbom/
#     license/version/benchmark/fuzz/release-dryrun/doctor recipes
#   * recommends `import "phenotype.just"` (path-submodule) as the default
#     layout; consumers can switch to `import "just/phenotype.just"` if
#     vendoring the library in-repo.

# Path to the shared library. Adjust if you vendor it under just/.
import "phenotype.just"

# === stack-specific recipes (examples) ===
# Uncomment / adapt the block that matches your stack. Add new blocks below;
# the shared library will never define these because they are non-portable.

# Register/refresh Windows Start-Menu shortcuts for Electrobun desktop apps.
# no-arg = all apps in Tools/apps.json; `just register-startmenu AppName` = one.
# BUILD HOOK: call this at the END of each `electrobun build` step so a
# completed build always re-points its shortcut at the latest output, e.g.:
#     electrobun build && just register-startmenu {{app}}
# register-startmenu app="":
#     pwsh -NoProfile -File Tools/Register-StartMenuApps.ps1 {{ if app == "" { "" } else { "-App " + app } }}

# Django: apply migrations against the configured database.
# migrate:
#     uv run python manage.py migrate

# Rails: drop, create, migrate, seed.
# db-reset:
#     bin/rails db:drop db:create db:migrate db:seed
